Package: pulzr-ap
Provides: parkeze-ap
Replaces: parkeze-ap
Conflicts: parkeze-ap
Depends: ucode, ucode-mod-uci, wpad-openssl, iw, dnsmasq-full, jsonfilter
Maintainer: Joseph Telaak <joseph@pulzr.net>
Architecture: all
Description: Setup access point.
 Raises a self-titled access point so a gateway can be reconfigured when it has
 dropped off the network, from the console, or from four presses of the reset
 button. Open only while the gateway has no credentials to lose; WPA2 with a
 per-device key once it is adopted.
 .
 Depends on wpad rather than hostapd and wpa-supplicant separately: wpad IS
 both daemons in one binary and CONFLICTS with each of them, so asking for
 hostapd-basic-openssl alongside the wpad the boards already pull in is an
 unsatisfiable package set. This package needs AP mode and station mode, which
 is exactly what wpad provides.
 .
 The full wpad, not wpad-basic: basic has no 802.1X, so a gateway could not
 join WPA2-Enterprise (eduroam, most campus and corporate WiFi). openssl
 rather than mbedtls: mbedtls 3.6.3 and later refuse to verify a server
 certificate without an expected hostname, and wpa_supplicant's mbedtls
 backend sets none, so every EAP handshake died before the certificate was
 reported. pulzr-wifi-probe never saw a chain, and a pinned join would have
 failed the same way. libopenssl3 is already in the image for openssl-util.
